<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-30T05:45:35Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Live: Several people killed as Russia launches new round of strikes on Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:815cc2f53acceaca7c7856de7002ab60998614d239dbdfba1575f32ca8b74755</id><updated>2026-09-30T05:45:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T05:35:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260930-live-several-people-killed-as-russia-launches-new-round-of-strikes-on-kyiv--16599397238f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260930-live-several-people-killed-as-russia-launches-new-round-of-strikes-on-kyiv" /><summary type="html">At least three people, including a child, have died after Russia launched another round of strikes on Kyiv and its surrounding regions overnight to Wednesday, officials said. Several people were also wounded in the attacks. In Poland, two airports, in Lublin and Rzeszow, were briefly shut over “military aviation activity” during Russian attacks on Ukraine. Follow our liveblog for all the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Heatwaves, wildfires expose a third of world to extreme ozone pollution</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7551a8f2eaa7b291f9fe2322a46d8ec5a892e9089144cb457cfd411ed22ac7fc</id><updated>2026-09-30T05:45:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T02:31:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/environment/20260930-heatwaves-wildfires-expose-a-third-of-world-to-extreme-ozone-pollution--6f8ca8388372.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/environment/20260930-heatwaves-wildfires-expose-a-third-of-world-to-extreme-ozone-pollution" /><summary type="html">Heatwaves and wildfires helped expose 34 percent of the world’s population to “extremely poor” ozone air quality in the first eight months of 2026, according to a European Union report published Wednesday. Asia recorded the highest exposure, while ozone pollution remained difficult to curb despite decades of progress in reducing other harmful emissions.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>US forces leave Iraq, raising fears of Iran-backed militias amid power vacuum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32b0963c8b00f135ce3a22ff25bd05d3ca823bb1b5ab6bed429af694a2181a58</id><updated>2026-09-30T05:45:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T01:04:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260930-us-forces-leave-iraq-raising-fears-of-iran-backed-militias-amid-power-vacuum--6f5d6f0a7ff6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260930-us-forces-leave-iraq-raising-fears-of-iran-backed-militias-amid-power-vacuum" /><summary type="html">US forces are withdrawing from their remaining bases in Iraq on Wednesday, completing a pullout agreed under former president Joe Biden as fears grow over the security vacuum it could leave. Iraqi officials and analysts warn the departure could embolden Iran-backed militias and give Islamic State group fighters room to rebuild their capabilities.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Still the same far-right? Le Pen's National Rally denies fresh antisemitism claims</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f87c59782ef34182472c23a01914c2709a7e7f7e5cf49186dce438905ca07453</id><updated>2026-09-30T05:45:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T23:19:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260929-still-the-same-far-right-le-pen-s-national-rally-denies-fresh-antisemitism-claims--ca8a9519ecb4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260929-still-the-same-far-right-le-pen-s-national-rally-denies-fresh-antisemitism-claims" /><summary type="html">Minor bump on the French far-right’s road to power—or a car crash that wipes out years of rebranding?
 
Bombshell allegations of past antisemitic tropes by the man Marine Le Pen has touted as her future prime minister could test her years-long effort to convince French voters that the National Rally is a party of government, rather than the fringe far-right National Front of old.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>US Supreme Court lifts restrictions on third-country deportations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9265e2f6a6ae72e132adc7d219049c29b80a93d302ccbefb2dffffe035dcba56</id><updated>2026-09-30T05:45:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T23:17:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260929-us-supreme-court-lifts-restrictions-on-third-country-deportations--2246aab0be9d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260929-us-supreme-court-lifts-restrictions-on-third-country-deportations" /><summary type="html">The US Supreme Court on Tuesday cleared the Trump administration to resume deporting migrants to countries other than their own while it considers the legality of the practice. The court’s conservative majority temporarily blocked safeguards requiring deportees to receive notice of where they would be sent and time to raise persecution concerns.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says AI companies sign voluntary accord on safety controls</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ccc967f56ab2627893a48d6ec59ffbb60caf1954da61f0598618be4395a9b74f</id><updated>2026-09-30T05:45:23Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T22:48:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/technology/20260929-trump-says-ai-companies-sign-voluntary-accord-on-safety-controls--e3b6a83a640c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/technology/20260929-trump-says-ai-companies-sign-voluntary-accord-on-safety-controls" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump and leaders of major artificial intelligence companies signed a voluntary accord Tuesday to strengthen safety reviews as the technology faces growing public concern. The agreement calls for internal controls, independent audits and board oversight, while Trump rejected calls for government restrictions and urged rapid AI development.</summary><category term="Technology" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says doesn't want to work with China on AI safety</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:74826c1b4ec3f3b3df47f0432b8314ee61a84365083d35a54de2692c7fd86be0</id><updated>2026-09-30T05:45:26Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T21:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260929-trump-says-doesn-t-want-to-work-with-china-on-ai-safety--f973a01a98ad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260929-trump-says-doesn-t-want-to-work-with-china-on-ai-safety" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump discussed AI development with dozens of tech bosses at the White House.  Ahead of his "superintelligence" luncheon, Trump launched a new AI-powered website for government services vowing not to stifle the technology's growth.  He also said he didn't want to work with Chinese President Xi Jinping on AI oversight. Plus, dozens of dogs were rescued from a breeding farm in South Korea as the country prepares for a complete phaseout of the dog meat industry.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Safeguards 'build a moat' around US AI firms, prevent open-source models from advancing, expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bb33d3174cf4d931ea447b6f0db2d2d8ccc0789644e5b6cc8815947e54642a60</id><updated>2026-09-30T05:45:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T21:00:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260929-safeguards-build-a-moat-around-us-ai-firms-prevent-open-source-models-from-advancing-expert--e4d6c568f5c0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260929-safeguards-build-a-moat-around-us-ai-firms-prevent-open-source-models-from-advancing-expert-says" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Tuesday said the tech executives gathered at the White House to discuss regulating AI had signed a "morally binding" commitment to build adequate safeguards on the fast-moving technology. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Monte Francis, Harrison Rolfes, Senior Research Analyst at PitchBook, says that the push for safeguards "prevents open-source models from taking over the competition as well as new incumbents from coming in with a new frontier model", explaining that the measures "build a moat" around US AI firms.</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Safeguards 'build a moat' around US AI firms, prevent open-source models from advancing, expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a27bb1a88c24085629f7e173ea4ca49fafaddc01a7dfc0d9dd79b57a736a8edd</id><updated>2026-09-30T05:45:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T20:58:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/safeguards-build-a-moat-around-us-ai-firms-prevent-open-source-models-from-advancing-expert-says--fe5c0950a31e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/safeguards-build-a-moat-around-us-ai-firms-prevent-open-source-models-from-advancing-expert-says" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Tuesday said the tech executives gathered at the White House to discuss regulating AI had signed a "morally binding" commitment to build adequate safeguards on the fast-moving technology. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Monte Francis, Harrison Rolfes, Senior Research Analyst at PitchBook, says that the push for safeguards "prevents open-source models from taking over the competition as well as new incumbents from coming in with a new frontier model", explaining that the measures "build a moat" around US AI firms.</summary></entry><entry><title>Public service announcement or Donald Trump propaganda?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:387bb2f301c524b32bccf959957b84084c6a77d48af60c82f998513d0e6a534c</id><updated>2026-09-30T05:45:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T20:56:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20260929-public-service-announcement-or-donald-trump-propaganda--6e88764ee389.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20260929-public-service-announcement-or-donald-trump-propaganda" /><summary type="html">The White House calls them public service announcements - like those used in past administrations. Almost everyone else doesn't agree, with three taxpayer-funded advertisements that glorify President Donald Trump drawing criticism from across the partisan divide. Legal experts say the ads violate federal laws on government propaganda, as France 24's Emerald Maxwell explains in this edition of Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>France intends to borrow record €340 billion as Covid-era debt comes due</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c7c8847de2244cf5357805590a7da326176ca0a8382ee5abad5da8ebf857f379</id><updated>2026-09-30T05:44:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T20:34:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/business/20260929-france-intends-to-borrow-record-340-billion-euros-covid-era-debt-comes-due--80c207ae93d4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/business/20260929-france-intends-to-borrow-record-340-billion-euros-covid-era-debt-comes-due" /><summary type="html">The French ​government will sell a record amount of bonds to investors next year as it faces a surge in Covid-era debt due for redemption and needing to be refinanced, the public debt management ​office ‌said on Tuesday amid mounting concern about France's surging public deficit and borrowing rates.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Ugandan coronation under social media scrutiny</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:019059309be04958fd380dabb9fd31f5d9eb02580fa97b42e36397d8214debe0</id><updated>2026-09-30T05:44:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T20:22:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ugandan-coronation-under-social-media-scrutiny--bc49397c37a1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ugandan-coronation-under-social-media-scrutiny" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, Uganda's new king of Tooro is crowned before thousands. Also, Africa's richest man cautions the continent against losing control of its major projects. And dozens of civilians are killed as Ethiopian government forces bombard towns in the northern region of Tigray.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>One in eight cancers worldwide linked to infections, WHO agency says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:50d298071457c47c943d1874dede55e7594884e0ea348666a9043dacadbf5c8e</id><updated>2026-09-30T05:44:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T20:03:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/one-in-eight-cancers-worldwide-linked-to-infections-who-agency-says--226c33f5354b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/one-in-eight-cancers-worldwide-linked-to-infections-who-agency-says" /><summary type="html">A new study from the International Agency for Research on Cancer (IARC) shows that an estimated 2.3 million new cancer cases worldwide in 2024 – about 12% of all new cancer cases – were caused by infections and could be prevented with treatment or vaccines. FRANCE 24's Jennie Shin speaks with the lead author of the study, Dr Gary Clifford, Scientist at the IARC.</summary></entry><entry><title>Mystery over UK airbase scare as police find 'quantity of petrol' but no explosives</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab2fcde077a722a5a8aa039d106eadfc7d20bfe566a5369552f0732f97ef8312</id><updated>2026-09-30T05:44:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T19:05:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260929-mystery-over-uk-airbase-scare-as-police-find-quantity-of-petrol-but-no-explosives--1845b2e97bf4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260929-mystery-over-uk-airbase-scare-as-police-find-quantity-of-petrol-but-no-explosives" /><summary type="html">Britain's counter-terrorism police said ​on Tuesday that no improvised explosive devices had been found as part of an ​investigation ‌into a suspected plot targeting ⁠a British airbase used by US forces to ‌strike Iran, deepening uncertainty over the incident a day after five UK-based suspects were released on bail.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Burnham sets out 'new path' for Britain, vows to seek consensus on ties with EU</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:524220b00fe9a369f187fad1d86ce9dc41e71d4c47a40f70192aa6b6db847e75</id><updated>2026-09-30T05:44:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T17:54:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260929-burnham-sets-out-new-path-for-britain-vows-to-seek-consensus-on-ties-with-eu--7d1bd2026ea1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260929-burnham-sets-out-new-path-for-britain-vows-to-seek-consensus-on-ties-with-eu" /><summary type="html">UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham pledged Tuesday to give Britain "a new social contract for the 21st century", reform the country's electoral system and build consensus on a new relationship with the European Union as he set out a long-term vision to tackle the UK's woes in his first speech as leader at the annual Labour party conference.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Marrakesh mayor Fatima Ezzahra El Mansouri becomes first woman prime minister of Morocco</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fa7b6a4629825618c3e0a1c094373b8acd596179bc9a79ac6332cfd2e46f1e38</id><updated>2026-09-30T05:44:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T16:09:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260929-morocco-king-appoints-first-woman-prime-minister-el-mansouri-after-parliamentary-vote--45f176d87012.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260929-morocco-king-appoints-first-woman-prime-minister-el-mansouri-after-parliamentary-vote" /></entry><entry><title>Morocco's king appoints Marrakesh mayor El Mansouri as first woman prime minister</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:de63c5fffa23f4a19b16c063be228f793247d7a749b02d4049b80aee7513c3d5</id><updated>2026-09-30T05:44:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T16:08:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260929-morocco-king-appoints-first-woman-prime-minister-el-mansouri-after-parliamentary-vote--45f176d87012.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260929-morocco-king-appoints-first-woman-prime-minister-el-mansouri-after-parliamentary-vote" /><summary type="html">King Mohammed VI appointed Fatima Ezzahra El Mansouri as Morocco's first woman prime minister on Tuesday after her liberal-centrist party came out on top in a September 23 parliamentary election, the royal palace said. Her government is expected to make major investments linked to the 2030 FIFA World Cup, while facing pressing issues including unemployment and living costs.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Legion of Honour: Police investigate corruption claims for France’s top award</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f5aac8e0cb8c5a46648c0723691ca829f1facfb630fe06c6156a25ee2dbf964f</id><updated>2026-09-30T05:44:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T14:43:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20260929-legion-of-honour-police-investigate-corruption-claims-for-france-s-top-award--807135d46c8c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260929-legion-of-honour-police-investigate-corruption-claims-for-france-s-top-award" /><summary type="html">French police took a top general into custody last week as part of an ongoing probe into potential bribery among the selection committee for the country’s highest decoration, the Legion of Honour. Investigations centre on possible payoffs for awards including expansive meals, holidays and thousands of euros in cash.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>A view from Brazil: The fight for the favela vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c483d371e850ac8a216ee763b8f41f2ed3d6996fed5fc33df35733d8a4221c74</id><updated>2026-09-30T05:44:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T14:41:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260929-a-view-from-brazil-the-fight-for-the-favela-vote--072d5fed5d09.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260929-a-view-from-brazil-the-fight-for-the-favela-vote" /><summary type="html">In Brazil, more than 158 million voters are being called to the polls on Sunday to elect their next president, as well as new members of Congress and governors. In Rio de Janeiro, local candidates are fighting for one particularly sought-after electorate: the residents of favelas. FRANCE 24’s Jan Onoszko reports from Rocinha, Brazil’s largest favela.</summary></entry><entry><title>French civil servants strike, demand additional budgetary resources</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1bc4544a3811e9b0242c4d76b6f3cf2d3d5af731163dcd8c9551085e389f99fd</id><updated>2026-09-30T05:44:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T14:40:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260929-french-civil-servants-strike-demand-additional-budgetary-resources--c949011e8342.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260929-french-civil-servants-strike-demand-additional-budgetary-resources" /><summary type="html">French civil servants were mobilising in large numbers on Tuesday, with more than 170 rallies planned across France. A coalition of unions are demanding additional budgetary resources for schools, hospitals, and other public services. Among those on strike are firefighters, pushed to their limits by the summer's historic wildfires. Here's a look at one of the protests in Lyon.</summary></entry><entry><title>Over 100 settlers attack Occupied West Bank village, clash with Israeli forces</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4609e67d46974fca88168a3f118206fee33543064011818cded07942da363d50</id><updated>2026-09-30T05:44:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T14:38:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260929-over-100-settlers-attack-occupied-west-bank-village-clash-with-israeli-forces--dcaf9d3f51b0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260929-over-100-settlers-attack-occupied-west-bank-village-clash-with-israeli-forces" /><summary type="html">More than 100 Israeli settlers attacked a village in the north of the occupied West Bank early Tuesday, wounding three members of Israel's security forces and burning two Palestinian homes, authorities and residents said. The attack occurred while the military was attempting to accompany a Palestinian family back to their home in the village of Jalud after they had been displaced by settler attacks two months earlier. ABC Journalist Jordana Miller reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Eiffel Tower chief to step down over removal of women staff during Hindu group's visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:119ca53c9ab7a5753ea272a73863b8c8ce0377a27e860d976905a36d904ec5bc</id><updated>2026-09-30T05:44:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T14:22:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20260929-eiffel-tower-chief-to-step-down-over-removal-of-women-staff-during-hindu-group-visit-baps--b41494b5c445.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260929-eiffel-tower-chief-to-step-down-over-removal-of-women-staff-during-hindu-group-visit-baps" /><summary type="html">The head of the Eiffel Tower is set to step down in the wake of a controversy sparked by the removal of female workers during a private visit of the Paris landmark by members of the Hindu sect BAPS, which triggered a staff walkout earlier this month and sparked outrage in France.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>French far-right leader Bardella denies anti-Semitism accusations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c658b74cbe1da9310f6afad56f3d76997ffb075abd667e8e7494b7a037addb71</id><updated>2026-09-30T05:44:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T14:11:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260929-french-far-right-leader-bardella-denies-anti-semitism-accusations--a91ccb3d8627.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260929-french-far-right-leader-bardella-denies-anti-semitism-accusations" /><summary type="html">🇫🇷 ✡️ Far-right #NationalRally (RN) party leader Jordan #Bardella has denied accusation by French investigative website #Mediapart that he made anti-Semitic comments on private chats in 2013. It comes as RN candidate Marine #LePen is polling well in the lead for the 2027 presidential election.</summary></entry><entry><title>France's Le Pen defiant after top ally hit by antisemitism claims</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a3aea8d5f28170dc49c296f8cd6c10c3df78f39e70e50bbcde43585cedfda130</id><updated>2026-09-30T05:44:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T14:10:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260929-france-s-le-pen-defiant-after-top-ally-hit-by-antisemitism-claims--98e92d9d0e0e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260929-france-s-le-pen-defiant-after-top-ally-hit-by-antisemitism-claims" /><summary type="html">French far-right presidential candidate Marine Le Pen on Tuesday vowed to hit back at allegations of antisemitism targeting her de-facto number two Jordan Bardella, which have punctured her buoyant campaign at a time she is riding high in the polls. Le Pen, who is aiming to win the Elysee at her fourth attempt next year in a far-right breakthrough that would send a shockwave across Europe, lambasted the Mediapart website that published the claims and said Bardella has her "total confidence".</summary></entry></feed>
